          %h2#motivation Motivation
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            is continuous but not cocontinuous functor. Hence the Grothendieck topologies are used to define smaller codomain of Yoneda, a sheaf subcategory of the category of presheaves such that for that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/corestriction"} corestricted
            Yoneda embedding (into sheaves) a desired class of covering cones will stay covering cones. More general families of diagrams than the sieves of a Grothendieck topology may be involved in achieving this. The important properties of the categories of diagrams for doing the sheaf theory can be expressed in terms of an adjoint pair of functors; this adjoint pair gives an example of a
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
